{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "day": 27,
  "level": 2,
  "title": { "en": "Winter clothes", "es": "La ropa" },
  "objectives": [
    "Name the clothes you'll pack for Madrid in January",
    "Ask for your size in a shop",
    "Say what you have and what you need with tengo and quiero"
  ],
  "teach": [
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**For the cold**\n\n- **el abrigo**: coat\n- **la bufanda**: scarf\n- **los guantes**: gloves\n- **el gorro**: woolly hat\n- **el jersey**: jumper, sweater\n\nMadrid in January is dry and sunny but cold: often around 0 °C in the morning and 10 °C in the afternoon."
    },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**Everyday clothes**\n\n- **la chaqueta**: jacket\n- **los pantalones**: trousers (always plural, like English)\n- **la camiseta**: T-shirt\n- **los zapatos**: shoes\n\n*La ropa* = clothes. It's singular in Spanish: *la ropa es bonita*."
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Tiene la talla cuarenta?", "en": "Do you have size 40?", "note": "La talla = clothes size. Spain uses European sizes. For shoes, say el número: ¿Tiene el número cuarenta y dos?" },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Quería un gorro y una bufanda.", "en": "I'd like a hat and a scarf.", "note": "Polite quería from day 16 works in shops, too." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Tengo frío. ¿Dónde está mi abrigo?", "en": "I'm cold. Where is my coat?", "note": "mi = my (mis for plural: mis guantes)." },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**Las rebajas.** Spain's winter sales start in early January. Shops choose their own dates, and most big Madrid stores begin right after Reyes (6 January), some a few days before. Either way, they'll be on when you arrive, and shop windows will say *REBAJAS* everywhere."
    }
  ],
  "vocab": [
